The crystal energy in an ionic compound is related to the electrostatic potential energy between the ions in the crystal lattice. The Madelung constant accounts for the geometry and arrangement of ions in the crystal structure.

The formula to calculate the crystal energy per mole is:

\[
\Delta E_{\text{cryst}} = -\frac{1}{2} N_A \cdot M \cdot \frac{Z^+ \cdot Z^- \cdot e^2}{4 \pi \epsilon_0 r_{\text{cation}} \cdot r_{\text{anion}}}
\]

